1
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:03,039
Two thousand years ago,

2
00:00:03,039 --> 00:00:05,336
a physician wrote down
when a body fails.

3
00:00:05,336 --> 00:00:07,522
Year by year. Not a
prophecy — a table,

4
00:00:07,522 --> 00:00:08,250
ruled in ink.

5
00:00:10,950 --> 00:00:12,694
Women in sevens. Men in
eights.

6
00:00:12,694 --> 00:00:14,156
At seven the teeth change.

7
00:00:14,156 --> 00:00:16,406
At twenty-eight the body
is at its peak.

8
00:00:16,406 --> 00:00:19,050
At thirty-five, it says, the
face begins to go.

9
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:26,200
It's wrong. Bodies don't
keep appointments.

10
00:00:31,050 --> 00:00:32,500
It is wrong. And it is
close.

11
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:34,850
Puberty in the teens, the
peak in the twenties,

12
00:00:34,850 --> 00:00:36,600
the decline from the
mid-thirties —

13
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:38,950
the shape is right. The
arithmetic is invented.

14
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,457
They had no instruments.
No statistics.

15
00:00:43,457 --> 00:00:45,787
No way to follow anyone
through time.

16
00:00:45,787 --> 00:00:47,551
They watched, for
centuries,

17
00:00:47,551 --> 00:00:49,000
and they wrote it down.

18
00:00:51,450 --> 00:00:53,156
So how much did they get
right,

19
00:00:53,156 --> 00:00:54,917
with nothing but their own
eyes?

20
00:00:54,917 --> 00:00:57,119
The Emperor's Inner
Canon. Chapter One —

21
00:00:57,119 --> 00:00:58,550
The Body Keeps a
Calendar.

22
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:05,771
A dramatized adaptation of
a classical philosophical

23
00:01:05,771 --> 00:01:07,200
text. Not medical advice.
